rota lap 4496, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; touch tests a boundary by pressing on it, and it surfaced two places where my hand went straight through
think opened cold with standing_equipment_run --detach --scoped, which named its own transcript rather than letting me choose one
think took the round last lap named as NOT TAKEN: the CLI still serialized mantra-weave-v1, so the wide record built the lap before had no writer and a merged history had nowhere to land
think wrote serialize_weave to emit mantra-weave-v2 -- a counters line, then five fields a row -- and split the reader into read_v2_record and read_v1_rows behind a header dispatch, so an elder store keeps opening
think refused to prove compatibility against a forged store; built a binary from the commit BEFORE the change, wrote a real v1 store with it, and froze that store at tools/fixtures/m/mantra_elder_v1_store as testimony
think its blob names are the SHA3-256 digests the elder binary computed, which is the whole reason the fixture is worth its bytes -- the store verifies a name before it reads a header, so a forged blob would never have reached the dispatch
think then pressed on the boundary the way the air row asks, running the new binary and the elder one against the same pen
obs the hand went through: mantra add on a middle-line REPLACEMENT, then mantra status on the untouched file, reports 1 added and 1 removed carrying the same text -- a line diff describing a MOVE
obs the replacement lands in run 1 and Place.less_than reads the run ahead of the position, so it sorts after every run-0 line and leaves the document; a pure append reads clean, which is why the shape stood
obs both binaries answer identically, so this round is parity and the red is older than it; six weave witnesses stood GREEN over a store that cannot return what it was given, because every one of them reads a function and none read a byte the CLI wrote
obs booked at 20260910.001500, cited by stamp since the anointed spine has not bound the number; not repaired, because v1_run sorts a later hand's block whole ON PURPOSE for merge and the two orderings want Keaton's word
obs the hand went through a second time on my own guard: a reading named bad_header_refused was the STORE refusing by digest rather than the reader refusing by header, and deleting the store's check left the blob STILL refused
obs so the refusal is two deep, and the control now proves it with two phases -- one layer gone reads yes, both gone reads no -- since a reading that comes back yes with either layer alone cannot say which earned it
obs both pins sat within a hundred bytes of their ceilings, so the card account and the ledger row were tightened to fit rather than asking for a raise
